cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this graph, its vocabularies or its code, please cite it as below."
title: "Bible Ontology"
abstract: >-
  A knowledge graph of what the text of the Bible says: its people, places,
  events and claims, each relation resting on the verses that establish it and
  credited to the voice that makes it, read from the Hebrew and Greek (MACULA)
  and shown in the Berean Standard Bible. Published with RDF vocabularies,
  SHACL shapes and an alignment to standard vocabularies.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Egge"
    given-names: "Doug"
url: "https://bibleontology.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bibleontology/bibleontology"
license:
